meta {
  name: CreateInvite
  type: grpc
  seq: 3
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.IdentityService/CreateInvite
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "email": "new.dev@company.com",
      "role": "ROLE_DEVELOPER",
      "grants": [
        { "resource": { "id": "res-github" }, "level": "use" }
      ],
      "idempotency_key": "{{$guid}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0017, convention 5). The `ctx` field the messages still declare is ignored
  by the server — do not use it: it gives the false impression of scoping the
  call.

  The role and the grants are composed IN THE INVITE — there is no default
  (ADR-0013). Whoever invites chooses: everything, nothing or a selection.

  The invite expires in 14 days and is revocable while pending.
}
